  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "On-resistance is guaranteed at two gate levels: 15 mΩ max at -10 V and 20 mΩ max at -4.5 V. The gate is rated to ±20 V and leaks at most ±100 nA there. Charging it to -10 V takes 110 nC typical with -30 V and -50 A at the drain; the gate-drain share of that is 28 nC, and the gate-charge curve holds flat near 3.7 V from about 19 nC to 47 nC. Gate-charge and switching-time figures hold at any operating temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "On-resistance climbs with junction temperature: about 1.3 times its 25 °C value at 75 °C and about 2 times at 175 °C. The guaranteed maximum with -10 V on the gate at -50 A is 25 mΩ at a 125 °C junction and 30 mΩ at 175 °C. Drain leakage at -48 V rises from 1 µA max at 25 °C to 50 µA at 125 °C and 150 µA at 175 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Current and heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 50 A continuous rating at a 25 °C case is a package limit; the case-temperature curve holds that level up to about 92 °C and falls to zero at 175 °C, passing 39 A at 125 °C. Dissipation is 136 W with the case held at 25 °C, but only 3 W at a 25 °C ambient on a 1 inch square FR4 board, where junction to ambient is 40 °C/W typical and 50 °C/W max in steady state (18 °C/W max for 10 s or less). Both dissipation figures derate with voltage along the safe operating area curve."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Avalanche",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part takes 50 A of avalanche current and 125 mJ of repetitive avalanche energy with a 0.1 mH inductor at a duty cycle of 1 % or less."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain diode carries 50 A continuous and 80 A pulsed. At 50 A its forward drop is 1 V typical, 1.6 V max, and it recovers in 45 ns typical, 70 ns max, at 100 A/µs. Diode figures are set by design rather than production tested."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Board footprint",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The minimum land pattern for the DPAK is a 5.690 mm by 6.180 mm pad under the tab and two 1.397 mm by 2.286 mm lead pads, 4.572 mm apart edge to like edge, 2.202 mm from the tab pad; it spans 10.668 mm overall."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package versions",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The TO-252AA outline comes from two factories with slightly different dimensions: version 1, facility code Y, and version 2, facility code N. On version 2, flash on the heat-sink side is at most 0.8 mm and the radius on the terminals is optional."
  }
